.TH smi-decrypt "1" "June 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Encryption Command"
.SH NAME
smi-decrypt \- Decrypt and verify a file encrypted with smi-encrypt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-decrypt
.I ENCRYPTED_FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-decrypt
decrypts the specified
.I ENCRYPTED_FILE
(usually with a
.B .enc
suffix) using OpenSSL with AES-256-CBC symmetric decryption.
The passphrase is read interactively from the terminal without echo.
.PP
Before decrypting,
.B smi-decrypt
verifies the HMAC-SHA-512 integrity tag stored in
.IR ENCRYPTED_FILE .hmac .
If the tag does not match, decryption is aborted and exit code
.B 3
is returned.
This detects both accidental corruption and intentional tampering.
.PP
Key derivation uses PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA-256 and 600\,000 iterations with the salt stored
in the encrypted file header, matching the parameters used by
.BR smi-encrypt (1).
.PP
The command is suitable for decrypting both
.B text and binary files
of any size.
There is
.B no upper limit on file size
imposed by the key or block size.
.PP
The passphrase is entered via the terminal (stdin) without any graphical or TUI pinentry dialog,
making the command safe to use over SSH and in non-graphical environments.
.PP
Upon successful decryption both
.I ENCRYPTED_FILE
and its
.I .hmac
file are removed and the original file is restored.
.PP
.B Note:
files encrypted with earlier versions of this tool (10\,000 iterations, no HMAC file) are not
compatible with the current version and must be decrypted with the matching older version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I ENCRYPTED_FILE
Path to the AES-256-CBC encrypted file to decrypt, typically produced by
.BR smi-encrypt (1).
Must be an existing regular file.
A corresponding
.I ENCRYPTED_FILE.hmac
integrity file must also be present.
Both files are removed after successful decryption.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
File decrypted successfully; encrypted file and HMAC file removed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid usage: wrong number of arguments, encrypted file does not exist, or HMAC file not found.
.TP
.B 2
Decryption failed.
.TP
.B 3
Integrity check failed: the HMAC does not match.
The file may be corrupted or tampered with.
No files are modified.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Decrypt a previously encrypted configuration file:
.IP
smi-decrypt secrets.conf.enc
.PP
The decrypted output is restored to
.IR secrets.conf .
Encrypt a file first with:
.IP
smi-encrypt secrets.conf
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
